            <h2 class="section-title">Why China Leads in Medicine</h2>
            <p class="section-lead">Independent evidence — not marketing. Here's what sets China's top hospitals apart from anywhere else in the world.</p>
            <div class="journey-grid">
                <div class="journey-card">
                    <div style="font-size:2em;margin-bottom:12px">🏆</div>
                    <h3>Fudan-Ranked Excellence</h3>
                    <p>China's hospital ranking system — the <strong>Fudan University Hospital Rankings</strong> — is the most rigorous in Asia. Departments are evaluated on clinical outcomes, research output, and peer reputation. Top-ranked departments in <strong>cardiac surgery, oncology, ophthalmology, and orthopedics</strong> compete with the best hospitals globally — and in many specialties, they lead.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="journey-card">
                    <div style="font-size:2em;margin-bottom:12px">🔬</div>
                    <h3>Technology at the Frontier</h3>
                    <p>China has <strong>7 approved CAR-T cell therapies</strong> — among the most of any nation — including the <strong>world's first CAR-T for solid tumors</strong> (satri-cel, approved June 2026). Chinese hospitals performed the <strong>first fully autonomous robotic dental implant</strong>, run some of the world's largest <strong>CRISPR clinical trial programs</strong>, and operate a rapidly growing network of <strong>proton therapy centers</strong>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="journey-card">
                    <div style="font-size:2em;margin-bottom:12px">👨‍⚕️</div>
                    <h3>Surgical Volume = Better Outcomes</h3>
                    <p>A surgeon at Fuwai Hospital performs <strong>over 15,000 cardiac surgeries a year</strong>. At Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, surgeons complete <strong>20,000+ refractive surgeries annually</strong>. This volume — <strong>5–10× what a typical Western surgeon handles</strong> — translates directly into fewer complications, shorter operating times, and faster recovery.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="journey-card">
                    <div style="font-size:2em;margin-bottom:12px">🌿</div>
                    <h3>Integrated Medicine — Unique to China</h3>
                    <p>No other country delivers <strong>acupuncture, herbal medicine, and Western surgery</strong> under one hospital roof as standard care. Chinese hospitals integrate TCM into oncology (reducing chemo side effects), orthopedics (accelerating post-surgical recovery), and cardiac rehabilitation. It's not alternative medicine — it's <strong>state-sponsored, evidence-based integration</strong>.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

